From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:11:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 118/148] test(refinery): pin reject mode of the acceptance
 check, red against b3b72667 (gcp-s7j4.4)

Reject mode is specified in the bead before it is built, so the suites that
prove it come first and fail for the reasons the bead names: record rejects
--mode reject as a usage error, the fence still says reject is not built yet,
there is no acceptance-reject block, and the formula has four stamp blocks.

test_refinery_acceptance_check.sh: the gc stub learns --status and --assignee
updates and a workflow arm, with the GC_STUB_FAIL_WORKFLOW and GC_STUB_FAIL_STATUS
knobs. New cases pin the full write order of a reject-mode MISS, that nothing
routes except that MISS, and a pool return that fails at delete-source or at the
status write. packet re-reads a bead that came back at the same tip after a
reject-mode MISS and still skips every other judged case. The text invariant
drops the four fragments reject mode now writes and keeps the ones that say
record never closes a bead or touches a molecule.

test_refinery_acceptance_wiring.sh: the reject-runs-as-warn case becomes a
reject-mode case, the fence pin carries the three edits to the fence, the prose
pin comes in three pieces, case_reject_block executes the new block against a
stub that answers per-id assignees, and case_head_left_pour holds the pour copy
byte-equal to the rebase step's.

test_refinery_restart_cadence.sh: the acceptance-check step is the fifth pour
that continues the conversation.

